<https://martial.is/entity/01M1CC980TYXQ77FNJFEVQ25D4>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://web.archive.org/web/20260930081140/https://budojapan.com/kenjutsu-iai/20231020smr/>;
        schema:datePublished            "2023";
        schema:description              "Budo Japan feature article (October 20, 2023) by Grigoris Miliaresis reporting on a visit to the\nYushinkan dojo, the headquarter Dojo of Shinto Munen-ryu. Covers the school's history from its\n18th-century founder Fukui Hyoomon through Negishi Shingoro's transformation of the Renpeikan\ninto the Yushinkan in 1885, and the school's 20th-century development under Nakayama Hakudo, who\nkept it alive through the pre-war, wartime and post-war periods. Confirms that Hakudo left the\nschool to his son Nakayama Zendo (1900-1981), 'one of the few people who inherited Hakudo's martial\nknowledge in its totality,' who in 1969 asked Ogawa Takeshi (then 24) to dedicate his life to the\nheritage as the 10th head. Includes photographs of Nakayama Hakudo and Nakayama Zendo, and detailed\ndescriptions of Shinto Munen-ryu kumitachi and iai kata.\n"@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "en";
        schema:keywords                 "article";
        schema:keywords                 "iaido";
        schema:keywords                 "yushinkan";
        schema:keywords                 "kenjutsu";
        schema:keywords                 "koryu";
        schema:keywords                 "nakayama-hakudo";
        schema:keywords                 "shindo-munen-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "nakayama-zendo";
        schema:keywords                 "iaijutsu";
        schema:name                     "Sword saints past and present - A visit to Shinto Munen-ryu's Yushinkan";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01M1CC980TYXQ77FNJFEVQ25D4/publisher>;
        schema:url                      <https://budojapan.com/kenjutsu-iai/20231020smr/>;
