        schema:description     "The branch of Ittō-ryū kenjutsu carried by the Nakanishi family; practitioners and the branch itself continued to call it \"Ono-ha Ittō-ryū\" (its formal lineage name), with \"Nakanishi-ha\" attaching as a common designation once headship had passed through several generations of the Nakanishi family. Takano Sakichirō, a senior disciple of the branch's 4th-generation head, and his grandson Takano Sasaburō both trained and taught in this line, which became a root of modern kendo pedagogy."@en;
