<https://martial.is/entity/01M0R2X2AC17096BKGZ28CK3GY>
        rdf:type               martialis:Person;
        schema:description     "Kendo kyoshi 7th dan and police dojo instructor in Tokyo, described by Japanese Wikipedia as Yukio Mishima's kendo master (kendo no shi). The Funasaka family's first-hand account records that Mishima started kendo under Yoshikawa at the Himonya Police Station in Meguro and followed him when Yoshikawa moved to teach at the Shibuya Police Station; Japanese Wikipedia likewise places Mishima's regular Sunday practice with him at Himonya, where he also began iaido. Tom Bolling's resume instead dates formal instruction to June 1958 at the Higashi-Chofu Police Station. It was through Yoshikawa's introduction that Mishima formally entered Omori-ryu iai under Funasaka Yoshio."@en;
        schema:keywords        "kendo";
        schema:name            "Yoshikawa Masami"@ja-Latn;
