        schema:description      "French master-at-arms in savate and canne who founded his own walking-stick and umbrella self-defence method around 1898 in Geneva, where he had a school of arms. He was the stick-fighting instructor of Barton-Wright's Bartitsu Club in London, opened his own academy at 18 Berner Street in 1903, and returned to Geneva in 1912. His wife Marguerite, his assistant instructor, developed an umbrella self-defence method."@en;
