<https://martial.is/entity/01M0TQQ4D975QSE0N8QCTF2K9W>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:alternateName    "Chinese wrestling"@en;
        schema:alternateName    "Kuai Jiao"@en;
        schema:alternateName    "Shuaijiao"@en;
        schema:description      "Shuai jiao is the ancient jacket-wrestling wushu style of China, with regional traditions in\nBeijing, Tianjin, Baoding (where the fast-throwing kuai jiao variant developed), and Shanxi.\nAncient Chinese wrestling terminology (jiaodi, jiaoli) is documented from the Zhou dynasty\nonward, and a widely repeated Republican-era account presents shuai jiao as its unbroken\ncontinuation - a narrative some read as a Han-nationalist revision\ndating to anti-Qing sentiment of the early 20th century. What is not contested is the\nQing-era institutional lineage: the Manchu adopted Mongol bökh as buku (布庫) and formed the\nShan Pu Ying (善撲營), an elite imperial wrestling battalion; after the dynasty's fall in 1912,\nformer battalion members taught Han and Hui civilians in Beijing, Tianjin, and Baoding. Ma\nLiang formalised the art in 1917 through the manual Zhonghua Xin Wushu (中華新武術), and the\nCentral Guoshu Institute fixed the name \"shuai jiao\" and standardised competition rules in\n1928. It remains a recognised discipline of Chinese wushu, governed alongside sanda by the\nsame national and international wushu bodies, and continues to be taught in Chinese police\nand military academies.\n"@en;
        schema:description      "摔跤是中國古老的著衣摔跤武術，有北京、天津、保定（快跤）、山西等地方傳統。清代滿族將蒙古式摔跤\n（博克）稱為布庫，並組建善撲營。1912年清朝滅亡後，善撲營成員向北京、天津、保定的漢族及回族平民\n傳授技藝。1917年馬良編著《中華新武術》使該武術系統化，1928年中央國術館確定「摔跤」之名並標準化\n比賽規則。摔跤現為中國武術的正式項目之一，與散打同受國家及國際武術機構管轄。\n"@zh;
        schema:image            <https://martial.is/entity/01M0TQQ4D975QSE0N8QCTF2K9W/photos/0>;
        schema:keywords         "shuai-jiao";
        schema:keywords         "wushu";
        schema:keywords         "wrestling";
        schema:keywords         "jacket-wrestling";
        schema:keywords         "chinese-martial-arts";
        schema:name             "Shuai Jiao"@en;
        schema:name             "Shuāijiāo"@zh-Latn;
        schema:name             "摔跤"@zh;
        schema:sameAs           <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q280502>;
