        schema:description             "Japanese judoka and jujutsuka. Founder of the Budokwai (1918), known as the 'Father of British Judo.' Studied Tenjin Shinyo-ryu under Nobushige Tago, later Shin-Shin-Ryu under Yamada Nobukatsu and Akishima-Ryu under Akishima Tsunejiro. Converted to Kodokan Judo in 1920 under Jigoro Kano. Co-founded the British Judo Association (1948) and European Judo Union (1948). Author of 'My Study of Judo' (1960). Held 8th dan Kodokan."@en;
        schema:name                    "小泉軍治"@ja;
        schema:name                    "Koizumi Gunji"@ja-Latn;
        schema:name                    "Gunji Koizumi"@en;
