<https://martial.is/entity/01M2Z6TY1P8PHZ6627T6GXFP6V>
        rdf:type                martialis:Place;
        schema:alternateName    "Mito Tōbukan"@en;
        schema:description      "水戸の私塾道場。1874年（明治7年）1月1日、小澤寅吉が自邸に開いた。北辰一刀流剣術・新田宮流抜刀術を指南し、 内藤高治・門奈正を輩出した。日本の三大私塾道場の一つ。"@ja;
        schema:description      "Private kenjutsu dojo in Mito, Ibaraki, opened 1874-01-01 by Kozawa Torakichi in his own residence after the abolition of the Mito domain. Taught Hokushin Ittō-ryū kenjutsu and Shin Tamiya-ryū battojutsu; Naitō Takaharu and Monna Tadashi trained there before going on to the Keishichō and the Butokukai. One of the three great private dojos of Japan (kenshi247); private ownership has continued in the Kozawa family, and the dojo still practises kendo, iaido, naginata, Hokushin Ittō-ryū, and Shin Tamiya-ryū (JA wiki, Mito Tobukan)."@en;
        schema:keywords         "hokushin-ritto-ryu";
        schema:keywords         "koryu";
        schema:keywords         "mito";
        schema:keywords         "dojo";
