<https://martial.is/entity/01M0AZQ3TJAG1RBRXBQJCRRJX6>
        rdf:type                       martialis:Person;
        schema:alternateName           "半田彌太郎"@ja;
        schema:alternateName           "Yataro Handa"@en;
        schema:birthDate               "1847";
        schema:description             "Japanese jujutsu master from Osaka, founder of Daito-ryu jujutsu (大東流柔術) and of the Seibukan dojo at\nDojima-ura-cho, Kita-ku, Osaka in 1878. Born in 1847 as the son of the Kishu domain retainer Taniguchi Toemon, he\ntrained in Sekiguchi Shinshin-ryu under Sekiguchi Ujitane (from 1860), in Tenjin Shin'yo-ryu under Yamana Shinkuro\n(山名新九郎) and in Shibukawa-ryu under Takenaka Isamu (竹中勇). After a warrior pilgrimage (musha shugyo) through Shikoku,\nKyushu, Chugoku, Omi and Yamashiro in 1874, he settled in Osaka in 1876, succeeding to the dojo of Yamana Shinjuro\n(山名新十郎) - a different, related figure from his teacher Yamana Shinkuro - and in\n1878 established the Seibukan and founded Daito-ryu jujutsu. His students included Uyenishi Sadakazu, Taro Miyake,\nYukio Tani and Seizo Yamamoto, who carried the school's ground-grappling skills to London from 1900. He was the\nsempai (senior) of the Fusen-ryu master Mataemon Tanabe, who cross-trained (degeiko) at the Seibukan from 1898 and\nregularly taught there. Despite the similar name, his Daito-ryu jujutsu is a separate school from the Daito-ryu\nAiki-jujutsu lineage of Takeda Sokaku.\n"@en;
        schema:description             "大東流柔術の開祖であり、1878年に大阪市北区堂島裏町に盛武館を開いた柔術家。1847年に紀州藩士・谷口藤右衛門の子として\n生まれ、関口新心流を関口氏胤（1860年より）、天神真楊流を山名新九郎、澁川流を竹中勇に学んだ。1874年の武者修行\n（四国・九州・中国・江州・山城）を経て、1876年に大阪に移り山名新十郎の道場を継ぎ、1878年に盛武館を開いて大東流柔術を\n創始した。門人には上西貞一・三宅多留次・谷幸雄・山本清蔵らがおり、1900年からロンドンでその寝技を伝えた。不遷流の\n田辺又右衛門は半田の先輩で、1898年から盛武館に出稽古し常時指導にあたった。名称が似るが武田惣角系の\n大東流合気柔術とは別流派である。\n"@ja;
        schema:keywords                "daito-ryu";
        schema:keywords                "osaka";
        schema:keywords                "jujutsu";
        schema:keywords                "japan";
        schema:name                    "半田 弥太郎"@ja;
        schema:name                    "Handa Yatarō"@ja-Latn;
