<https://martial.is/entity/01M5JSGG506VYDX6SQPQ4CFV6W>
        rdf:type                martialis:Person;
        schema:alternateName    "Angelo Viggiani"@en;
        schema:alternateName    "Angelus Viggianus"@en;
        schema:description      "Bolognese fencing master and innovator whose Lo Schermo, a dialogue finished about 1551 and printed in 1575, recast the theory of the Bolognese school: the sword alone, seven guards with the right foot forward, rational names for the guards, and the thrust on the lunge as the perfect attack."@en;
