<https://martial.is/entity/01KJJAWN29MA64W22606R3WD73>
        rdf:type                martialis:Person;
        schema:description      "Japanese jujutsuka who, with Takitaro Taki, brought jujutsu to Portugal (Lisbon, late 1909), then acted in\nPorto (16 Jun - mid Aug 1910) against Yamaguchi among others. Possibly the smallest Japanese wrestler of the era\n(1.45 m, 50 kg). Married Phoebe Laughton Parry (the British women's jujutsu pioneer, covered here as Phoebe\nRoberts) in March 1907; the couple demonstrated at the Palace Theatre, Manchester in 1908, where Phoebe was billed\nas 'Miss Roberts, Lady Champion Ju-jitsu Wrestler of the World'. Hirano founded a Ju-jitsu Academy in Barcelona in\n1909, then moved to Portugal with Phoebe, teaching the PSP police in Porto and training Armando Gonçalves.\nPer Callan/Heffernan/Spenn (2019) he is thought to have drowned off Santa Cruz beach, Portugal in 1915, his body\nnever found; Phoebe remarried (Carlos de Castro Henriques) in 1916. Gonçalves's own books (1914, 1936, 1941,\n1942) attest his discipleship under Hirano.\n"@en;
        schema:description      "Mestre japonês de jujutsu que, com Takitaro Taki, trouxe o jujutsu a Portugal (Lisboa, finais de 1909) e depois\natuou no Porto (16 de junho - meados de agosto de 1910), entre outros contra Yamaguchi. Casou com Phoebe Laughton\nParry, antiga aluna de Raku em Londres, e fixou residência com ela no Porto, onde ensinou a PSP e treinou Armando\nGonçalves.\n"@pt;
        schema:name             "Hirano Yuzo"@ja-Latn;
        schema:nationality      <https://martial.is/entity/01KJJAWN29MA64W22606R3WD73/nationality/0>;
        martialis:hasEvidence   <https://martial.is/entity/01KJJAWN29MA64W22606R3WD73/hasEvidence/2>;
