<https://martial.is/entity/01KZF4BJ5E12C1517S2ZMXP8YV>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <http://web.archive.org/web/20250210054250/https://www.bushidoreiryokukan.com.au/master-seiichi-akamine/>;
        schema:description              "Biography of Seiichi Akamine (1920-1995) by Sensei Roberto Fernandez de la Reguera (his Chile representative, translated by Christian Tapia), from the Bushido Reiryoku Kan school. Primary descendant account: born Naha 14 May 1920, early training under his grandfather, Shorin-ryu under Chomo Hanashiro, Kentsu Yabu and Chotoku Kyan, then Goju-ryu under Seiko Higa and Kanki Izumigawa (1st dan at 16, 2nd at 18, 4th at 22 from Higa), kobudo under Shinko Matayoshi, Tokyo years (Shikan-kan dojo, anatomy/physiology studies), the 1950 Nippon TV demonstration, immigration to Brazil in 1957, the Brazilian Association of Karate-Do, the Ken-Shin-Kan school (1968), and his Chile/Uruguay branches. Received 8th dan from the Japanese Butokai and declined 9th and 10th dan."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "en";
        schema:keywords                 "goju-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "karate";
        schema:name                     "Master Seiichi Akamine - Bushido Reiryoku Kan";
