        schema:description              "English Wikipedia article on jodo, the Japanese martial art of the short staff (jo). Gives the art's two names - jodo, \"way of the jo\", and jojutsu, \"art of the jo\" - notes its similarity to bojutsu and its strong focus on defence against the Japanese sword, and gives the jo's length as roughly 3 to 5 feet. Also recounts the Shinto Muso-ryu founding tradition of Muso Gonnosuke Katsuyoshi and his duels with Miyamoto Musashi, including the shortening of the bo to a 4 shaku 2 sun 1 bu jo."@en;
