        schema:datePublished            "2020";
        schema:description              "Peer-reviewed academic article (Martial Arts Studies, no. 10, pp. 66-72) by David Brough on the dojo Uyenishi\nestablished at 31 Golden Square, Piccadilly Circus in 1903. Focuses on Uyenishi's teaching of the British Army\nand of women's classes, and how these influenced physical culture and laid the foundation for the politicisation\nof jujutsu as women's self-defence. Notes Uyenishi left the UK in 1907 and that the dojo lived on through William\nand Edith Garrud before being demolished by 1930.\n"@en;
