<https://martial.is/entity/01M0SP452BBXZZ00G6ZZFJHH1D>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://ja.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=%E5%B1%B1%E6%9C%AC%E8%88%9C%E5%8B%9D&oldid=108631472>;
        schema:description              "Japanese Wikipedia article on Yamamoto Kiyokatsu (1919-2001), career army officer (major, Nakano School intelligence instructor) and postwar GSDF lieutenant general-rank officer at the Ground Self- Defense Force Intelligence School (Kodaira, Tokyo), where he helped create its psychological warfare defence course, served as education section chief from March 1967 and deputy commandant from July 1969, retiring in February 1972. Known as the de facto instructor of Mishima's Tatenokai, leading their guerrilla-warfare lectures, street exercises and infiltration drills, and opposing the final coup plan. Lists his memoirs on Mishima, including Jieitai \"Kage no Butai\" (Kodansha, 2001)."@en;
