<https://martial.is/entity/01KZHA2591TZDF7ARNDGNTC1KC>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <http://web.archive.org/web/20250917152223/https://tourism.odks.jp/en/post-7.html>;
        schema:description              "Okinawa Dento Karatedo Shinkokai tourism page on the Nagamine Shoshin monument in Tomari, Naha. States Nagamine, born in Tomari, began his martial arts journey under Chojin Kuba of Tomari-te, then Taro Shimabukuro of Shuri-te, and ultimately Ankichi Aragaki, a disciple of Kyan Chotoku; while stationed at Kadena Police Station he studied under Kyan Chotoku for approximately two years; created the \"popular kata I\" in 1941; in 1997 became the first individual in the Okinawan karate community designated \"Okinawa Prefecture's Intangible Cultural Property Holder.\""@en;
