<https://martial.is/entity/01KZH6AA1PF3CKXMWN6YZXGD7H>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://ja.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=%E7%9F%A5%E5%BF%B5%E8%BC%9D%E5%A4%AB&oldid=111435378>;
        schema:description              "Japanese Wikipedia article on Teruo Chinen (1941-2015), Goju-ryu karate master who founded the Jundokan International karate organization. Born in Kobe, Hyogo (the lead gives July 8, 1941 while the body gives June 8, 1941); father a Japanese Navy officer from Okinawa, grandfather a full-time te instructor, great-grandfather in the Yamane-ryu kobudo lineage. Began Goju-ryu training in 1954 under Eiichi Miyazato; promoted to black belt after about six years; joined Morio Higaonna at the Yoyogi Dojo in Tokyo in 1959; went to Spokane, Washington in 1969 as technical advisor, promoted to 4th dan before departure; IOGKF technical advisor 1979-1986; founded Jundokan International in 1987; promoted to 7th dan by Miyazato around 1988; suffered undiagnosed diabetes from 1995."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "ja";
        schema:keywords                 "goju-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "wikipedia-ja";
