<https://martial.is/entity/01M6BQSYG6THHQB5HMBW87F6FE>
        rdf:type                       martialis:Person;
        schema:alternateName           "Yun K’wae Pyŏng"@en;
        schema:alternateName           "Yun Kwae-byung"@en;
        schema:alternateName           "Yun Kwei Byung"@en;
        schema:birthDate               "1919";
        schema:description             "Korean karate teacher. He studied Shurite karate under Tōyama Kanken at the Shūdōkan and in 1940 founded the Kanbukan in Tokyo, a sister school of the Shūdōkan known for full-contact sparring in bōgu. Back in Korea he joined the Chosŏn Yŏn-Mu Kwan, and in 1951 took over the school from Chun Sang-sup and renamed it Jidokwan. He brought bōgu sparring to Korean taekwondo."@en;
