        schema:description              "Portuguese translation of two articles on Eiichi Miyazato (1921-1999 per this source): \"The Final Interview!\" by Jaromir Musil (October 5, 2006) and an interview by Kent Moyer (2001). Primary accounts: Miyazato began training with Chojun Miyagi in 1935 at age 13; he was active in judo, All Okinawan Judo champion and president of the Okinawa Judo Federation; member of the board of directors of the All Japan Karate-Do Goju-Kai; 10th dan Hanshi and director of the Jundokan. Discusses the senior students of Miyagi at his death in 1953 (Seiko Higa, Meitoku Yagi, Eiichi Miyazato, Koshin Iha, Seikichi Toguchi) and the succession question."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "pt";
        schema:keywords                 "goju-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "karate";
        schema:name                     "A entrevista final com Eiichi Miyazato, fundador da escola Jundokan de Goju-Ryu";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01KZH5KBKXBXT04JW7BSZWXW1R/publisher>;
