<https://martial.is/entity/01KZKTQXG6C4K9JH93JHWKWT14>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <http://web.archive.org/web/20260823120616/https://tairafrance.fr/kenkyukai/>;
        schema:description              "Official page of the French branch of the Okinawa Goju Ryu Kenkyukai, a global karate organisation promoting research into the practical application of Okinawa Goju Ryu Karate kata and technique, headed by Taira Masaji Sensei, 9th Dan Hanshi. Confirms Taira Masaji (平良 正次, born 1 December 1952) as a leading teacher of Okinawa Goju Ryu Karate Do and head of the Okinawa Gojuryu Kenkyu Kai; his teacher was Eiichi Miyazato, a student of Chojun Miyagi and founder of the Jundokan; his karate is that of his teacher and the Jundokan with the addition of his novel approach to kata application, and he is best known as a researcher and practitioner of Goju Ryu kata bunkai. Records that he teaches seminars worldwide (US, Canada, Australia, France, Italy, Portugal, England, Lithuania, India and New Zealand) and that the French branch is represented since 2012 by OGKKF Paris (Pascal Duroux and Christian Rosso) and IGKDF Vanves (Nirina Rakotozafiminahy)."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "en";
        schema:keywords                 "website";
        schema:keywords                 "goju-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "karate";
        schema:name                     "Goju Ryu Kenkyukai - Taira Kenkyukai France";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01KZKTQXG6C4K9JH93JHWKWT14/publisher>;
        schema:url                      <https://tairafrance.fr/kenkyukai/>;
        martialis:accessed              "2026-09-23";
        martialis:sourceClassification  srcclass:authored;
        martialis:sourceType            "webpage" .

