<https://martial.is/entity/01KZH6AA1PBR5EVSWHMWSA39QT>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://web.archive.org/web/20261018124139/https://shuriway.com/tchinen.html>;
        schema:description              "Shuriway biography of Teruo Chinen (1941-2015) by Leonardo Pereira, president of Jundokan International in Portugal. Born June 8, 1941 in Kobe; family moved to Shuri at five and Naha at six; grandfather a Shorin-ryu instructor and father practiced bo, sai and nunchaku; influenced by the school next door, Chojun Miyagi's dojo. Began training in 1954 under Eiichi Miyazato at the Jundokan dojo; after five years left for Tokyo, joining Morio Higaonna in 1959; trained together five years and developed randori. In 1969 came to Spokane as technical advisor to the Spokane School of Karate; IOGKF technical advisor 1973-1984; formed Jundokan International in 1984 in honor of his teacher Eiichi Miyazato."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "en";
