        schema:description      "One of the oldest surviving Japanese martial arts (天真正伝香取神道流), founded by Iizasa Ienao, who was born in 1387 in Iizasa village and lived near Katori Shrine. The school dates its founding to 1447, though some scholars give about 1480. Kenjutsu is its core, with battōjutsu, ryōtōjutsu, bōjutsu, naginatajutsu, sōjutsu, shurikenjutsu and jūjutsu also taught."@en;
