<https://martial.is/entity/01M3287E2AS86XZ08PV8EH76E2>
        rdf:type                    martialis:Person;
        schema:alternateName        "Takano Mitsumasa"@en;
        schema:alternateName        "苗正"@ja;
        schema:birthPlace           <https://martial.is/entity/01M3287E2AS86XZ08PV8EH76E2/birthEvent/birthPlace>;
        schema:deathDate            "1884-09";
        schema:description          "Kenjutsu instructor of Nakanishi-ha Ittō-ryū and grandfather of Takano Sasaburō, who trained his grandson in the style from early childhood. Born into the Horiuchi family of Ōno-hara village, Chichibu district, and adopted into the Takano family. Went to Edo and entered the Itto-ryu Nakanishi dojo, where he became a senior disciple of the 4th-generation head of Nakanishi-ha Itto-ryu (中西子正; ja.wikipedia's dedicated article on him gives this name and generation, while the English-language kenshi247 biography of his grandson instead names his teacher \"Nakanishi Chubei Tanemasa,\" described as a direct disciple of the 4th Ono-ha sōke, Ono Tadaichi - the two accounts do not fully agree on the intermediate teacher's identity or exact generation). Received menkyo kaiden in the style, then returned home to serve as kenjutsu instructor to the Oshi domain (忍藩) and ran a small dojo on the grounds of Chichibu Shrine."@en;
        schema:keywords             "itto-ryu";
