<https://martial.is/entity/01KZ6XT5DS0JHX51MN07878ERB>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:description      "Modern Japanese budo of drawing the sword and responding at once to a sudden attack, trained mostly alone through kata against imagined opponents. A kata runs through the draw (nukitsuke), the cut (kiritsuke/kirioroshi), shaking off the blood (chiburi) and the return to the scabbard (noto). The word 'iaido' dates from 1932 and was popularised by Nakayama Hakudo; the art grew from koryu iaijutsu, including Musō Jikiden Eishin-ryū, Mugai-ryū, Shindō Munen-ryū, Suiō-ryū and Hōki-ryū."@en;
        schema:description      "Budo japonês moderno de desembainhar a espada e responder de imediato a um ataque súbito, treinado sobretudo a solo, em kata contra adversários imaginários. Um kata percorre o saque (nukitsuke), o corte (kiritsuke/kirioroshi), o gesto de sacudir o sangue (chiburi) e o regresso à bainha (noto). A palavra 'iaido' data de 1932 e foi popularizada por Nakayama Hakudo; a arte nasceu do iaijutsu koryu, incluindo Musō Jikiden Eishin-ryū, Mugai-ryū, Shindō Munen-ryū, Suiō-ryū e Hōki-ryū."@pt;
        schema:image            <https://martial.is/entity/01KZ6XT5DS0JHX51MN07878ERB/photos/0>;
        schema:keywords         "iaido";
        schema:keywords         "japanese-martial-arts";
        schema:keywords         "gendai";
        schema:keywords         "swordsmanship";
        schema:name             "Iaido"@en;
        schema:name             "Iaidō"@ja-Latn;
