<https://martial.is/entity/01M764AMRBRPM8SE2D8A9D54RE/hasConfidence>
        rdf:type                       martialis:Confidence;
        prov:wasAttributedTo           <https://martial.is/agent/FSM>;
        martialis:assessedBy           <https://martial.is/agent/FSM>;
        martialis:confidenceLevel      conflevel:probable;
        martialis:confidenceRationale  "Pranin states Inoue learned Daitō-ryū from Takeda in Shirataki, and in the 1988 interview Pranin reports Inoue's name and seal in Takeda's enrolment book, which Inoue confirms - but Inoue denies that Takeda taught him, he says he refused Takeda's training and signed only after taking ukemi for him. JA Wikipedia says he never enrolled (possibly missing the interview). Inoue concedes signing, paying and a week of practice, so the denial is over the word \"taught\": a short formal enrolment, not a student relation. We have, on one hand, complete admission of all formalities of a teaching relation, while a negation of the actual content of that relation. Covering the \"quality\" of instructions is not within our scope, merely establishing that it existed, and all things considered, the relation is at least probable, verging on confirmed.        " .

