<https://martial.is/entity/01KZ6XT5DS3B4WD16YM3B0VK1M>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Iaijutsu&oldid=1376569959>;
        schema:description              "English Wikipedia article on iaijutsu, the combative quick-draw sword technique and one of the koryu disciplines of the classical warrior. Notes the term emerged from earlier sword-drawing practice (with battojutsu as an older name), its counter-attack orientation, Draeger's two starting postures (iai-goshi, tachi-ai), and the koryu schools that include iaijutsu (Muso Jikiden Eishin-ryu, Suio-ryu, Mugai-ryu, Tenshin Shoden Katori Shinto-ryu, Hoki-ryu and others). States that iaijutsu preceded and coexists with the modern form iaido (term first appearing in 1932)."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "en";
        schema:keywords                 "reference";
        schema:keywords                 "secondary-source";
        schema:name                     "Iaijutsu";
