        schema:alternateName   "Grappling"@en;
        schema:description     "Wrestling here denotes the Western/international grappling lineage\nthat converged into the modern Olympic and folk wrestling forms - Greco-Roman, freestyle,\nfolkstyle, catch, and submission wrestling. It is one of the oldest human combat disciplines,\nappearing in the ancient Olympic Games in 708 BC. National and regional wrestling traditions\noutside this lineage - Chinese shuai jiao, Mongolian bökh, Japanese judo and sumo, and others -\nare separate styles, even though English usage sometimes groups all of them under the single word \"wrestling\".\n"@en;
