<https://martial.is/entity/01M5JGQAC7D74DPNQ9EN4PW2JX>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:alternateName    "Baritsu"@en;
        schema:alternateName    "New Art of Self Defence"@en;
        schema:description      "Eclectic self-defence method announced by E. W. Barton-Wright in London in 1898. It began from the jujutsu he had studied in Kobe and, by 1901, cross-trained jujutsu, English boxing, savate, Pierre Vigny's walking-stick method and European wrestling, each for a different range of combat. It was taught at the Bartitsu Club in Soho until 1902–1903, then fell out of use; Conan Doyle's \"baritsu\" kept the name alive, and the Bartitsu Society has revived it since 2002."@en;
