        martialis:confidenceRationale  "English Wikipedia states the Beijing lineage is \"in essence the lineage from the Manchu buku style that was practiced by the Imperial Guards Brigade, Shan Pu Ying\" - Manchu buku being their adoption of Mongol bökh. Beijing shuai jiao elder Li Baoru is separately reported stating shuai jiao \"comes directly from Mongol Bokh\". Held at Probable rather than Confirmed because this is one side of a live historiographical dispute: the competing claim of an unbroken multi-millennial Han lineage from jiaodi/jiaoli is the mainstream popular account in Chinese-language sources." .

