        schema:description              "French Wikipedia article on Yoseikan Budo, covering the meaning of the name and logo, the technique repertoire, the 'wave' (mouvement ondulatoire) principle, the claim that the method is not a synthesis of existing arts, the uniform blue gi with blue and white belt, competition, the World Yoseikan Federation, and the 2000 soke succession. Records the art as developed in the late 1960s and officially founded in 1975 by Hiroo Mochizuki. Note: the article carries a 'needs more citations' banner."@en;
