        schema:archivedAt               <https://web.archive.org/web/20260429051747/https://revistas.unileon.es/ojs/index.php/artesmarciales/article/view/8452>;
        schema:datePublished            "2024";
        schema:description              "Peer-reviewed article by Carl De Crée on the historical roots of gonosen-no-kata, Revista de Artes Marciales Asiáticas 19(2), 129-150. Its author biography is the source for De Crée's own statements that he has studied judo with, inter alia, Felix De Smedt, Marcel Clause, Hirano Tokio, Fukuda Keiko, Imamura Haruo, Abe Ichirō, Daigo Toshirō and Ōsawa Yoshimi, that he holds 8th dan and the title of kyōshi, and that he is the first and only non-Japanese ever to hold menkyo in Kitō-ryū."@en;
