<https://martial.is/entity/01KYHF558ACS4T9K0BR6YWXABY>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:alternateName    "Tumai-dii"@ja-Latn;
        schema:description      "Tomari-te was a martial art tradition originating from Tomari village (present-day Naha City), the second-largest trading port of the Ryukyu Kingdom. Associated teachers include Matsumora Kosaku, Oyadomari Kokan, and Teruya Soeun Kishin (1804-1864). It is one of the three regional Okinawan te traditions - alongside Shuri-te and Naha-te - from which modern karate styles descended; it contributed to the development of Wado-ryu and branches of Shorin-ryu, including Matsubayashi-ryu."@en;
