        martialis:quotation        "Another Japanese jujutsu expert brought to the UK by Barton-Wright was the young Tani Yukio, who arrived in September 1899 with his elder brother. Tani performed extensively alongside Uyenishi in theatres such as the Tivoli. In 1902, he split with Barton Wright and was promoted in the music halls by William Bankier, otherwise known as Apollo. By 1904, Tani was also teaching at the Golden Square School.";
