<https://martial.is/entity/01M0AAFQFSD0PC83N17N4J3JXN>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:alternateName    "Fusen Ryu"@en;
        schema:description      "Fusen-ryu (不遷流) is a koryu school of jujutsu founded by Motsugai Takeda (also known as Fusen). Its curriculum\ncovers jujutsu, bojutsu, jojutsu, kenjutsu, iaijutsu, naginatajutsu, kusarigamajutsu and jittejutsu. Although\npopularly believed to be specialized in newaza (groundfighting) because of its famous master Mataemon Tanabe,\nthe style actually focused on gyaku-waza (stand-up grappling), especially wrist locks; Tanabe's ground strategy\ncame from his personal contest experience. The school rose to fame in 1891 when headmaster Tanabe defeated Kodokan\njudoka Takisaburo Tobari in a challenge match, and Tanabe taught at both the Dai Nippon Butoku Kai and Yataro\nHanda's Osaka dojo. Its most known apprentices were Taro Miyake and Yukio Tani.\n"@en;
        schema:image            <https://martial.is/entity/01M0AAFQFSD0PC83N17N4J3JXN/photos/0>;
        schema:keywords         "koryu";
        schema:keywords         "jujutsu";
