<https://martial.is/entity/01M5JG4Y25QKEKJ5K0T4KFYQW0>
        rdf:type                       martialis:Person;
        schema:alternateName           "Joseph Pierre Charlemont"@en;
        schema:birthDate               "1839-04-12";
        schema:birthPlace              <https://martial.is/entity/01M5JG4Y25QKEKJ5K0T4KFYQW0/birthEvent/birthPlace>;
        schema:deathDate               "1929-09-15";
        schema:deathPlace              <https://martial.is/entity/01M5JG4Y25QKEKJ5K0T4KFYQW0/deathEvent/deathPlace>;
        schema:description             "French boxing and canne master who codified the academic form of French boxing. He learned the Joinville method in the army and taught at Arras from 1862, building on the methods of Louis Vigneron, with whom he trained from 1861, and Charles Lecour. After the Commune he was in exile in Brussels, where he wrote his first book (1878). Back in Paris he founded the Académie de boxe in 1887 and published L'art de la boxe française et de la canne in 1899. His son Charles succeeded him."@en;
        schema:description             "Maître de boxe française et de canne qui en codifie la forme académique. Formé à la méthode de Joinville, il enseigne à Arras dès 1862 une méthode fondée sur celles de Louis Vigneron, avec qui il s'entraîne dès 1861, et de Charles Lecour ; exilé à Bruxelles après la Commune, il fonde à Paris l'Académie de boxe en 1887. Son fils Charles lui succède."@fr;
        schema:keywords                "savate";
        schema:keywords                "france";
        schema:keywords                "canne-de-combat";
        schema:name                    "Joseph Charlemont"@fr;
        schema:name                    "Joseph Charlemont"@en;
