        schema:description             "Australian middleweight boxer and teacher, \"Father of Australian Boxing\", a protégé of Jem Mace. After beating Abe Hicken in 1879 he opened a boxing academy at his White Horse Hotel in Sydney, with Mace as an instructor, introduced the Queensberry Rules to Australia, and trained Bob Fitzsimmons, Peter Jackson, Young Griffo and Frank Slavin. He controlled Australian boxing into the early 1900s."@en;
