        schema:birthPlace              <https://martial.is/entity/01KYS8C0AF6DD44239NY1DZ286/birthEvent/birthPlace>;
        schema:description             "Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu grandmaster and member of the Gracie family. Son of Hélio Gracie, he is widely regarded as one of the greatest BJJ practitioners of all time. Undefeated in MMA (11-0, all by submission), he won the Vale Tudo Japan tournament in 1994 and 1995, and defeated Nobuhiko Takada at Pride 1 and Pride 4. He is president of the Jiu-Jitsu Global Federation (JJGF) and features in the documentary Choke (1999).\n"@en;
