        martialis:confidenceRationale  "Baidu Baike states Li Junfeng studied in the wushu department at Beijing Physical Education Institute, 1960-1965, and was selected for the institute team. Zhang Wenguang chaired that department and specialised in Cha Quan, but no source names him as Li Junfeng's teacher." .

<https://martial.is/entity/01KZHA2591PCNFTPDK7CDQHVFC>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://ja.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=%E9%95%B7%E5%B6%BA%E5%B0%86%E7%9C%9F&oldid=109586288>;
        schema:description              "Japanese Wikipedia article on Nagamine Shoshin (1907-1997), Okinawan karateka, policeman, founder of Matsubayashi-ryu and karate historian. Born in Tomari, Naha; began karate at 17; studied under Ankichi Arakaki (a senior student of Kyan) from 19; graduated the Naha Commercial School in 1928 and joined the infantry (Jinan Incident); appointed policeman in 1931, studying under Kyan at Kadena Police Station; studied under Motobu Choki in Tokyo in 1936; awarded Renshi by the Dai Nippon Butokukai in 1940 (with Higa Seko); created the \"Fukyugata I\" in 1941; first vice chairman of the Okinawa Karate-do Federation 1956, chairman 1961-1969; organized the World Matsubayashi-ryu Karate Federation 1977; Order of the Rising Sun, 5th class (1982); designated an Okinawa Prefecture Intangible Cultural Asset holder in 1997, the first in the Okinawan karate world; died of acute renal failure the same year."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "ja";
        schema:keywords                 "matsubayashi-ryu";
