<https://martial.is/entity/01KYHQNWJF0CZFH1SXM9J40XEJ>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:alternateName    "Kuoshu"@en;
        schema:alternateName    "Gong fu"@en;
        schema:alternateName    "Wushu"@en;
        schema:alternateName    "Kung fu"@en;
        schema:description      "Chinese martial arts, commonly referred to with the umbrella terms kung fu, gong fu, kuoshu\nor wushu, are multiple fighting styles that have developed over the centuries in Greater\nChina, encompassing striking systems, jacket wrestling, and weapon arts. The striking\ntradition is broadly classified into internal (neijia) and external (waijia) schools, with\nmajor groupings including Wudang (internal) and Shaolin (external); alongside it sits shuai\njiao, China's native jacket-wrestling tradition, governed by the same national and\ninternational wushu bodies as the striking styles.\n"@en;
        schema:description      "中國武術是中國傳統武術的總稱，歷史悠久，流派眾多，涵蓋拳術、摔跤（摔跤）和器械武術。\n拳術主要分為內家拳和外家拳兩大類，其中內家拳以武當拳為代表，外家拳以少林拳為代表；\n摔跤則是中國本土的跤術傳統，與拳術同受同一武術管理機構管轄。\n"@zh;
        schema:image            <https://martial.is/entity/01KYHQNWJF0CZFH1SXM9J40XEJ/photos/0>;
        schema:keywords         "gong-fu";
        schema:keywords         "kuoshu";
        schema:keywords         "kung-fu";
        schema:keywords         "wushu";
        schema:keywords         "chinese-martial-arts";
        schema:name             "中國武術"@zh;
        schema:name             "Chinese martial arts"@en;
        schema:sameAs           <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3705105>;
