        schema:description              "Essay on a Mongolian-wrestling research site arguing, via Beijing shuai jiao elder Li Baoru's own testimony, that modern jacketed shuai jiao descends directly from Mongol bökh (via Manchu buku and the Qing Shan Pu Ying), and characterising the competing unbroken-Han-lineage narrative as a Republican-era, ethnonationalist revision. Self-published; cited for a contested minority position, not as an uncontested fact - see the confidence rationale on the citing assertion."@en;
