<https://martial.is/entity/01M2411V8RP1A9854ERZ2NQ80P>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:description      "Kyūdō (弓道) is the Japanese martial art of archery, practised with the asymmetrical\nwakyū (Japanese bow) of over two metres, gripped at the lower third of the stave. It\nis based on kyūjutsu, the archery art of the samurai class of feudal Japan; the name\nwas officially changed from kyūjutsu to kyūdō in 1919, and, following the example of\nother martial arts systematizing for educational purposes, the various forms of\nshooting in use until then were reorganized and integrated. Alongside its budo\ncharacter as training of body and mind, kyūdō today also carries the aspects of a\nsport and of school physical education. Practitioners may refer to themselves as\nyumihiki (弓引き), \"ones who draw the bow\".\n"@en;
        schema:image            <https://martial.is/entity/01M2411V8RP1A9854ERZ2NQ80P/photos/0>;
        schema:keywords         "archery";
        schema:keywords         "kyudo";
        schema:keywords         "japanese-martial-arts";
