<https://martial.is/entity/01M0T8BCW0Y9SZAN5KXZ7C4ZYW>
        rdf:type               martialis:Person;
        schema:description     "Kendoka and owner of the Taiseido martial-arts bookshop in Shibuya, Tokyo; elder brother of the Omori-ryu iai master Funasaka Yoshio. He was Mishima's senior at the kendo dojo they both attended, and after Mishima wrote a laudatory preface to his wartime memoir Eirei no Zekkyo (Cries of the Heroic Dead, 1966), he let Mishima choose a sword from his collection in September 1966 - a blade attributed to Seki no Magoroku that Japanese Wikipedia records he had bought from Nakamura Yasuichiro for 50,000 yen, though Christopher Ross's interviewee judged it a second-generation Kanemoto. The sword was used in the Ichigaya incident of 25 November 1970."@en;
