<https://martial.is/entity/01KZH9CVMEHQYXEP0PHH409T30>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://ja.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=%E7%A5%96%E5%A0%85%E6%96%B9%E7%AF%84&oldid=109242573>;
        schema:description              "Japanese Wikipedia article on Soken Hohan (1891-1982 per this source), Okinawan karateka active before and after the war, founder of Shorin-ryu Matsumura Seito. Born 1891 in Gaja, Nishihara; his mother Kami was a granddaughter of Matsumura Sokon; studied tōde under his maternal uncle Nabe Tanmei from about age 12 until 1918, then learned Ryukyu kobudo from Komesu Ushi Tanmei of Iho beach, Nishihara. Performed at the 1924 Taisho Theater demonstration in Naha with Motobu Choyu and Kyan Chotoku; emigrated to Buenos Aires in 1924 (photographer, then cleaner); returned to Okinawa in 1952; named his style Shorin-ryu Matsumura Seito karate-do around 1956; Okinawa Karate-do Federation director 1959; co-founded the Okinawa Kobudo Association in June 1961 with Uehara Seikichi, Shimabuku Tatsuo, Shimabukuro Zenryo and others. Died November 30, 1982."@en;
