        rdf:type                  martialis:Organization;
        schema:alternateName      "Beijing Martial Arts Association"@en;
        schema:description        "Municipal-level wushu sports association in Beijing, founded in 1962. One of the first provincial-level wushu associations established after the founding of the People's Republic. Organizes wushu competitions, training, and international exchange in the Beijing area. Currently led by President Lu Xuefeng (2025-present). Has 64 specialized committees, 21 working committees, and 93 member units. Notable officers include Vice Chairman Chang Zhenfang (from 1962) and Special Advisor Wu Bin."@en;
