<https://martial.is/entity/01KZXXSB98G9EWV0HR390VXFX4>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://web.archive.org/web/20130927195911/http://www.judo-karatemechelen.be/historiek.html>;
        schema:datePublished            "2006";
        schema:description              "History page of the Bushido-Kwai Mechelen club website on founder Felix De Smedt: his judo and jiu-jitsu instructor diploma from the school of Erich Rahn in Berlin, further training under Jean De Herdt (5th dan, European champion), Robert Godet (5th dan), G. F. M. Schutte (7th dan) and Tokio Hirano (7th dan, world champion), the founding of the Judo & Jiu-Jitsu Academie Bushido-Kwai at Schelle on 20 May 1946 at age 23, its expansion with branches at Boom, Willebroek, Mechelen, Heist o/d Berg, Weerde and Berlaar, the creation of the Mechelen branch on 14 March 1951, the Mechelen police-corps training, and consultation of master Ichiro Abe on the dojo tatami floor."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "nl";
        schema:name                     "Club historiek - Felix De Smedt, stichter van de Judo-Karate Academie Bushido-Kwai";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01KZXXSB98G9EWV0HR390VXFX4/publisher>;
