<https://martial.is/entity/01KZM518KZFC3R1B9VVFS90HBF>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <http://web.archive.org/web/20260810015950/http://findingkarate.com/wordpress/ansei-ueshiro/>;
        schema:description              "Biography of Ansei Ueshiro on the Finding Karate site. States he was born April 20, 1933 in Kin, Okinawa, son of Anch Ueshiro, descended from the Bushi warrior class, and nephew of the renowned karate master Ankichi Arakaki. He learned karate from his father and received lessons from Entasu Isaenta and Toguichi Seitoku. During the 1945 Battle of Okinawa his parents died and he lost several fingers on both hands with severe burns; around 1946 relatives enrolled him at the original Naha dojo of Shoshin Nagamine (himself a top student of Arakaki Ankichi). Records his 1960 promotion to 3rd dan by Nagamine and his eventual role as Chief Instructor of the dojo; the American serviceman James Wax as the first American promoted to black belt in Matsubayashi-Ryu Shorin-Ryu (1958), his marriage to Nagamine's niece and sponsorship of Ueshiro's move; Ueshiro's arrival in the United States on September 15, 1962, sent by Nagamine to spread Matsubayashi-Ryu; his first students James Wax and Frank Grant; the East Coast and Midwest schools by the late 1960s-70s; his departure from the central Matsubayashi-Ryu organisation in 1969 over disagreements following his creation of the Fukyugata Sandan kata; the establishment of Ueshiro Shorin-Ryu Karate USA by the 1980s; the 30-year celebration in 1992; and his death from a stroke on May 7, 2002 in Oceanside, New York, buried in Locust Valley, with Robert Scaglione continuing the organisation."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "en";
        schema:keywords                 "matsubayashi-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "website";
        schema:keywords                 "shorin-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "karate";
        schema:name                     "Ansei Ueshiro";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01KZM518KZFC3R1B9VVFS90HBF/publisher>;
        schema:url                      <http://findingkarate.com/wordpress/ansei-ueshiro/>;
        martialis:accessed              "2026-09-23";
        martialis:partOf                <https://martial.is/entity/01M64QW2FNVW32XVEJ4452RT2D>;
        martialis:peerReview            <https://w3id.org/martialis/vocab/peer-review/not_peer_reviewed>;
        martialis:sourceClassification  srcclass:authored;
        martialis:sourceType            "webpage" .

<https://martial.is/entity/01KZ6KZZG76Q52KMPKJRPG8001>
        rdf:type                       martialis:Person;
        schema:birthDate               "1937";
        schema:description             "Japanese aikido teacher (born 1937), a direct disciple of Morihei Ueshiba and uchi-deshi at the Aikikai Hombu Dojo from 1959 until the Founder's death in 1969. Promoted to 6th dan (Shihan) in 1968, he was Chief Weapons Instructor at Hombu until 1975, when he relocated to Sarasota, Florida, and founded the Aikido Schools of Ueshiba."@en;
        schema:description             "Professor japonês de aikido (nascido em 1937), discípulo direto de Morihei Ueshiba e uchideshi no Aikikai Hombu Dojo de 1959 até à morte do Fundador em 1969. Promovido a 6º dan (Shihan) em 1968, foi instrutor-chefe de armas no Hombu até 1975, quando se mudou para Sarasota, Flórida, e fundou a Aikido Schools of Ueshiba."@pt;
        schema:keywords                "uchi-deshi";
