<https://martial.is/entity/01M0AAFQFVW0M9K10ERYBCKH8H>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:alternateName    "Shinden Fudo-ryu"@en;
        schema:alternateName    "Immovable Heart School"@en;
        schema:description      "Shinden Fudo-ryu (神伝不動流, Immovable Heart School) is a koryu school of Japanese martial arts founded in around\n1113 by Izumo Kanja Yoshiteru, one of the oldest styles of jujutsu. The curriculum is entirely unarmed, with no\nweapons and no formal stance (kamae); techniques start from a natural, loose posture and work with one's natural\nsurroundings, most training taking place outdoors. It was a blend of indigenous Japanese and Chinese styles.\nNote that the Wikipedia article distinguishes the Shinden Fudo-ryu Dakentaijutsu lineage from the \"Shinden Fudo\nryu Kempo\" studied by Edward William Barton-Wright, which it says is not connected to the Dakentaijutsu school;\nthe BJS paper (citing Keegan 2019) nonetheless credits Barton-Wright with teaching Shinden Fudo-ryu jujutsu\ntechniques.\n"@en;
        schema:keywords         "koryu";
        schema:keywords         "jujutsu";
        schema:keywords         "japan";
        schema:name             "神伝不動流"@ja;
        schema:name             "Shinden Fudō-ryū"@ja-Latn;
        schema:sameAs           <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3482172>;
