        schema:description              "George W. Alexander's article on Hohan Soken (1889-1982), based on an interview conducted September 10, 1978. Born May 25, 1889 in Gaja Village, Nishihara City; founder of Matsumura Seito Shorin Ryu. States the Matsumura family lineage passed from Matsumura Sokon to his grandson Nabe Matsumura (1860-1920), and that Soken began training at thirteen in 1902 under his uncle Nabe Matsumura, his uncle's only student; after ten years of basic training began learning hakutsuru in 1912 at twenty-three. Also trained with Kenwa Mabuni and Gokenki (white crane), and studied weaponry under Komesu Ushi-no-Tanmei and Mantaka Tsuken. Moved to Buenos Aires in 1924, returning to Okinawa in 1952."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "en";
        schema:keywords                 "article";
        schema:keywords                 "shorin-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "karate";
        schema:name                     "Hohan Soken: The Life of a Grand Master";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01KZH9CVME1HC9XQTPH42B96FP/publisher>;
        schema:url                      <https://worldbudokan.com/worlbudokanhome/articles-2/hohan-soken/>;
        martialis:accessed              "2026-10-18";
        martialis:archiveDate           "2025-07-08";
        martialis:hasContributor        <https://martial.is/entity/01KZH9CVME1HC9XQTPH42B96FP/hasContributor/0>;
        martialis:sourceClassification  srcclass:authored;
        martialis:sourceType            "article" .

