<https://martial.is/entity/01M2Z12AZA53BW9KZHC2GD7PH1>
        rdf:type                       martialis:Person;
        schema:alternateName           "Ozawa Torakichi"@en;
        schema:alternateName           "Kozawa Masakata"@en;
        schema:birthDate               "1830";
        schema:birthPlace              <https://martial.is/entity/01M2Z12AZA53BW9KZHC2GD7PH1/birthEvent/birthPlace>;
        schema:deathDate               "1891";
        schema:description             "Mito-domain retainer and swordsman (Hokushin Ittō-ryū, Shin Tamiya-ryū), given name Masakata. Kenjutsu professor at the domain school Kōdōkan; reportedly trained under Chiba Shusaku (JA wiki, 'according to accounts'). After the abolition of the han, opened the Tōbukan dojo in his own residence on 1874-01-01, teaching Hokushin Ittō-ryū kenjutsu and Shin Tamiya-ryū battojutsu, and produced Naitō Takaharu and Monna Tadashi (JA wiki, Kozawa Torakichi). Inducted into the All Japan Kendo Federation's Kendo Dendō in 2005."@en;
        schema:description             "水戸藩士。藩校弘道館の剣術方教授。廃藩後、1874年（明治7年）1月1日自邸に道場・東武館を開き、北辰一刀流剣術・新田宮流 抜刀術を指南。内藤高治・門奈正を輩出した。2005年（平成17年）、剣道殿堂顕彰。"@ja;
        schema:keywords                "hokushin-ritto-ryu";
