<https://martial.is/entity/01KYHT5WPXM8YSZH28CGZ9DCA6>
        rdf:type                       martialis:Person;
        schema:alternateName           "Hwang Gi"@en;
        schema:birthDate               "1914-11-09";
        schema:birthPlace              <https://martial.is/entity/01KYHT5WPXM8YSZH28CGZ9DCA6/birthEvent/birthPlace>;
        schema:deathDate               "2002-07-14";
        schema:description             "South Korean martial artist, founder of the Moo Duk Kwan, the only one of the five original kwan founders who never trained in Japan. He said he learned a Chinese martial art from Yang Kook-jin in Manchuria and taekkyon as a child; both claims are disputed. Lee Won-kuk claimed Hwang trained at his Chung Do Kwan. By his own writings he learned karate from books. He called his art hwasu-do, from 1947 Tang Soo Do, and from the late 1950s Soo Bahk Do. His system influenced American Tang Soo Do through his student Shin Jae Chul."@en;
        schema:keywords                "korean-martial-arts";
