<https://martial.is/entity/01M1PBN7GAW97H77EV97J2JKYD>
        rdf:type                    martialis:Person;
        schema:birthDate            "1912";
        schema:description          "American judo pioneer and author born in 1912. He began practicing judo in the late 1920s and became an early instructor of the art in the United States. He taught judo at Queens College and at various YMCA clubs in the New York City area. He served as vice-chairman of the National AAU Judo Committee and was awarded a second-degree black belt by the Kodokan in Tokyo. Yerkow published six books on judo, including the three-volume Modern Judo series (Basic, Advanced, and 40 Gokyo Techniques), Sport Judo, Judo Katas, and Official Judo. Emilio Bruno described him in a 1972 letter as \"one of our very excellent judo pioneers\" who \"published the first judo book in the U.S. during World War II.\""@en;
        schema:keywords             "usa";
        schema:keywords             "author";
        schema:keywords             "pioneer";
        schema:keywords             "judo";
        schema:name                 "Charles Yerkow"@en;
        schema:nationality          <https://martial.is/entity/01M1PBN7GAW97H77EV97J2JKYD/nationality/0>;
