<https://martial.is/entity/01KZF0ZCDK22K38WTXS3634KAH>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://web.archive.org/web/20260726190207/https://fightingarts.com/seikichi-iha/>;
        schema:description              "Compilation of interviews with Seikichi Iha conducted between 1985 and 1992 at the Original Okinawa Karate dojo and Iha's home in Lansing, Michigan. Primary source: Iha born in Nishihara, Okinawa on July 12, 1932; trained under Shinpan Gusukuma (accepted as formal student in 1950, four years of training); after Gusukuma's death in 1954 met and studied under Katsuya Miyahira; promotions 5-dan shihan (1963), 6-dan (1964), kyoshi 7-dan (1967), kyoshi 8-dan (1978), hanshi 9-dan from Miyahira on March 12, 1989; teaching in Manila (1963-64), Futenma Marines (1964), Los Angeles (1967), and Lansing, Michigan (from 1975). US Branch Chief of the Okinawa Shorin-ryu Karatedo Association."@en;
