        schema:description              "Japanese Wikipedia article on Arakaki Seisho (1840-1920), Tote (karate) master of the late Ryukyu Kingdom and Meiji period and leading Naha-te master. Born 1840 in Higashi-wakasa-machi, Naha; nicknamed \"Mayaa Arakaki\" (Cat) or \"Arakaki Guwa\"; studied Tode under the Tei-shi Yabu Pechin (formerly Hokama); demonstrated the kata Jusanpo, Chishiyaukin and kumite at the 1867 celebration at the royal villa in Shuri; possibly accompanied the Shō Tai tribute mission to Beijing in 1867; Fumura Chikudon Pechin and Higaonna Kanryo are said to have studied under him. Note: gives death year 1920, differing from the EN Wikipedia 1918."@en;
