<https://martial.is/entity/01M07HCGJGXD0E7F4NBAK647YY>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:datePublished            "2013";
        schema:description              "Kindle biography of Edith Garrud (1872-1971), the first British female jujutsu teacher and trainer of the WSPU\nBodyguard, by Tony and Karen Wolf. Widely cited in the later academic literature: Brough (2020) draws on it for\nthe Garruds' training at the Bartitsu club and Golden Square Dojo, Edith's teaching of women's and children's\nclasses, her dojo at 9 Argyll Place, the red jacket she wore to stand out on stage, her sheltering of wanted WSPU\nmembers (1911-13), and the Garruds' retirement from teaching around 1925.\n"@en;
