<https://martial.is/entity/01M0AZQ3TJKDFZYF8638Y2992P>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:alternateName    "Daito-ryu Jujutsu"@en;
        schema:description      "Daito-ryu jujutsu (大東流柔術) is a koryu school of jujutsu founded by Handa Yataro (半田弥太郎) in Osaka in 1878.\nHanda trained in Sekiguchi Shinshin-ryu, Tenjin Shin'yo-ryu and Shibukawa-ryu, and devised the curriculum largely\nfrom Tenjin Shin'yo-ryu, with which it shares many technique names. He opened the Seibukan dojo at Dojima-ura-cho,\nKita-ku, Osaka and established the school together with the Daito Bunbukan. Its students - Uyenishi Sadakazu,\nTaro Miyake, Yukio Tani and Seizo Yamamoto - took the school's ground-grappling skills to London and the wider\nWest from 1900, and the Fusen-ryu master Mataemon Tanabe cross-trained (degeiko) at the Seibukan, whose instruction\nlater passed to Tanabe's student Fushimi Tatsusaburo. Despite the similar name, it is a different school from the\nDaito-ryu Aiki-jujutsu lineage of Takeda Sokaku.\n"@en;
        schema:description      "大東流柔術は半田弥太郎が1878年に大阪で開いた柔術の古流流派。半田は関口新心流・天神真楊流・澁川流を修行し、\n特に天神真楊流から技を考案したとされ、多くの技名が天神真楊流と共通する。大阪北区堂島裏町に盛武館を開き、\n大東文武館とともに大東流柔術を興した。門人の上西貞一・三宅多留次・谷幸雄・山本清蔵らは1900年からロンドンなど\n海外にその寝技を伝え、不遷流の田辺又右衛門も盛武館に出稽古に通い、後に田辺の門人伏見辰三郎が半田の後を継いだ。\n名称が似るものの武田惣角系の大東流合気柔術とは別流派である。\n"@ja;
        schema:keywords         "koryu";
        schema:keywords         "jujutsu";
        schema:keywords         "japan";
        schema:name             "大東流柔術"@ja;
        schema:name             "Daitō-ryū Jūjutsu"@ja-Latn;
        schema:sameAs           <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q109369448>;
        martialis:foundedEvent  <https://martial.is/entity/01M0AZQ3TJKDFZYF8638Y2992P/foundedEvent>;
        martialis:hasEvidence   <https://martial.is/entity/01M0AZQ3TJKDFZYF8638Y2992P/hasEvidence/1>;
