<https://martial.is/entity/01M5JSGG50SFSZ8CE3WR46RWC6>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:alternateName    "Bolognese swordsmanship"@en;
        schema:alternateName    "Dardi school"@en;
        schema:description      "The fencing tradition of Bologna, named after Lippo (Filippo) Dardi, who opened a school there in the 1410s. It taught armed and unarmed combat with the single-handed side sword and its companion arms, two-handed swords and polearms, with many guards, long solo drills and paired sequences. It is known from the sixteenth-century books of Guido Antonio de Luca's students Manciolino and Marozzo, and from Viggiani; Agrippa and the rapier masters grew out of it."@en;
        schema:image            <https://martial.is/entity/01M5JSGG50SFSZ8CE3WR46RWC6/photos/0>;
