        schema:description              "English Wikipedia article on Muso Jikiden Eishin Ryu, a Japanese iaijutsu school descended from Hayashizaki Jinsuke. Covers its history in the Tosa domain under the Yamauchi clan, the role of Oe Masaji in restructuring the curriculum, the two main branches (Tanimura-ha and Shimomura-ha), and notable teachers including Hosokawa Yoshimasa and Goto Magobei Masasuke. Oe Masaji was the second person after Nakayama Hakudo to be awarded hanshi in iaido by the Dai Nippon Butoku Kai."@en;
