<https://martial.is/entity/01M1CC980TYXQ77FNJFEVQ25D5>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://ja.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=%E4%B8%AD%E5%B1%B1%E5%96%84%E9%81%93&oldid=90325225>;
        schema:description              "Japanese Wikipedia article on Nakayama Zendo (1900-1981), eldest son and designated successor of Nakayama\nHakudo. Covers his birth as Nakayama Yoshimichi, his training at the Yushinkan dojo under his father in\nShindo Munen-ryu kenjutsu, Muso Shinden-ryu iaido, and Shindo Muso-ryu jodo, his Butokukai ranks (Seirensho\n1925, Kyoshi in iaido and jodo 1927, Kyoshi in kendo 1929), his succession as the 8th headmaster of Shindo\nMunen-ryu after Hakudo's death in 1958, his temporary retreat from the martial arts world during the\nwar and post-war period, and his later interviews that formed the basis of the Nakayama Hakudo Kendo\nKojutsushu. Includes external identifiers: ISNI 0000000381367172 and VIAF 260804040.\n"@en;
