<https://martial.is/entity/01M11YJ1XMX79NAEPJ09NWKC1S>
        rdf:type                     martialis:RankingSystem;
        schema:description           "The Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu ranking system, standardised by the IBJJF: eight named belts (white, blue, purple, brown, black, red-and-black, red-and-white, red), not a numbered dan/kyu ladder - belt colour is the rank itself, not insignia on top of one. Belt is the system's primary axis; each belt up to black further divides into numbered degrees (stripes); black belt divides into six degrees, after which the 7th/8th/9th degrees are marked by the red-and-black, red-and-white, and red belts respectively (10th degree red reserved for the art's founders)."@en;
