<https://martial.is/entity/01KZKYMMAGHXSMYTT70564YAE6>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://ja.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=%E6%9C%AC%E9%83%A8%E6%9C%9D%E5%9F%BA&oldid=109242076>;
        schema:description              "Japanese Wikipedia article on Motobu Choki (本部朝基, 1870-1944), Ryukyu Tode karateka and founder of Nihon Denryu Heiho Motobu Kenpo (Motobu-ryu). Gives the birth as Meiji 3, 4th month, 5th day (lunar) = May 5, 1870 (solar), third son of Motobu Aji Choshin in Shuri Akahira; childhood name Shinzaburo, nicknames \"Saru Gomen\" and \"Motobu no Saru\". Details the Motobu Udundi royal lineage (descendant of Sho Shitsu's sixth prince, Motobu Prince Chōhei); karate from age 12 under Itosu Anko with elder brother Choyu, then Matsumura Sokon and Sakuma Pechin, then Matsumora Kosaku (kumite); kake-dameshi at Tsuji; 1921 move to Osaka; November 1922 victory over a foreign boxer in Kyoto at age 52, covered by King magazine (September 1925 issue, the first to sell over a million copies); 1923 Tode-jutsu Fukyukai in Osaka; 1926 first kumite book Okinawa Kenpo Tode Jutsu Kumite-hen (the Choki 12 yakusoku kumite); 1927 move to Tokyo with the Daidokan dojo, Toyo University first shihan (1929), Otsuka Hironori became a student (1929); 1932 book Watashi no Todejutsu (Naihanchi photos); the Piston Horiguchi episode; kata repertoire (Naihanchi, Passai, Seisan, Channan, Hakugyoku); 1936-37 return to Okinawa; the October 25, 1936 Roundtable of Karate Masters; 1941 final return to Okinawa; death April 1944; students including Marukawa Kenji, Nakata Mizuhiko, Takano Genjuro, Higashionna Hiroshi, Sodeyama Toyosaku, Ueshima Sannosuke, Miyahira Katsuya and Nakama Chomo; the style continued by his son Motobu Chosei."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "ja";
        schema:keywords                 "motobu-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "wikipedia-ja";
        schema:keywords                 "karate";
        schema:name                     "本部朝基";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01KZKYMMAGHXSMYTT70564YAE6/publisher>;
