<https://martial.is/entity/01KZEV344570PFVXKKNTX5GYQP>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <http://web.archive.org/web/20260418232124/https://seibukan.info/history.html>;
        schema:description              "Official history of the Seibukan school on the International Okinawa Shorin-Ryu Seibukan Karate-do Association website. Covers founder Zenryo Shimabukuro (1909-1969): born Showa-era Shuri Kubagawa, Naha on November 5, 1909 (Meiji 42); to Osaka at 18 (1926); settled in Chatan 1933 as a confectioner; began training under Chotoku Kyan in 1935 (Showa 10); opened a dojo in Chatan in 1952; instructed US Army 503rd Airborne from 1961; built the Seibukan dojo in 1962, creating the Wanshu kata; president of the Okinawa Karate-do Union 1965; awarded Hanshi 10th dan by the All-Okinawa Karate Federation in 1967; died at 61 in 1969. Also covers successor Zenpo Shimabukuro (b. 1943), who studied Kobayashi-ryu under Chozo Nakama and inherited the school in 1969."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "ja";
        schema:keywords                 "seibukan";
        schema:keywords                 "shorin-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "karate";
        schema:keywords                 "official";
        schema:name                     "少林流聖武館歴史 - 国際沖縄少林流聖武館空手道協会";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01KZEV344570PFVXKKNTX5GYQP/publisher>;
        schema:url                      <https://seibukan.info/history.html>;
        martialis:accessed              "2026-09-23";
