<https://martial.is/entity/01KZKRQQR8B552430QEDYSNQQQ>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://web.archive.org/web/20261018122341/https://isshin-concentration.blogspot.com/2019/07/an-interview-with-katsuhiko-shinzato.html>;
        schema:datePublished            "2019";
        schema:description              "Translation (posted July 15, 2019 on the Isshin - Concentration the Art blog) of an interview with Katsuhiko Shinzato published in the Slovenian newspaper Dnevnik, conducted during his seminar visit to Slovenia (with his Okinawan students, at the invitation of Borut Mauhler); the interview dates to around 2010, as Shinzato mentions that the Encyclopaedia of Okinawan karate and kobudo (Kashiwashobo, Tokyo) was published the previous month. Shinzato states he entered the University of the Ryukyus in 1957 and began karate then, continued at a graduate school in the US, that the master with the greatest influence on him was Chokei Kishaba (dates given as 1931-2000), and that the study circle \"Kishaba Juku\" is named in honor of Kishaba's unique training methods. He was one of the contributors to the Encyclopaedia, whose information gathering began in 2003, and practices karate most days for six hours."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "en";
        schema:keywords                 "matsubayashi-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "shorin-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "karate";
        schema:name                     "An Interview with Katsuhiko Shinzato - Kashiba Juku";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01KZKRQQR8B552430QEDYSNQQQ/publisher>;
        schema:url                      <https://isshin-concentration.blogspot.com/2019/07/an-interview-with-katsuhiko-shinzato.html>;
        martialis:accessed              "2026-10-18";
        martialis:archiveDate           "2026-10-18";
        martialis:earliestYear          2019;
        martialis:latestYear            2019;
        martialis:partOf                <https://martial.is/entity/01M64QW2FNDSCYHEDGPM8JY0FD>;
        martialis:peerReview            <https://w3id.org/martialis/vocab/peer-review/not_peer_reviewed>;
        martialis:sourceClassification  srcclass:derivative;
        martialis:sourceGenre           <https://w3id.org/martialis/vocab/source-genre/interview>;
        martialis:sourceType            "interview" .

<https://martial.is/entity/01KZ6D9E8Q3F78F13SS130W679>
        rdf:type                martialis:Place;
        schema:description      "The Budo Club du Maroc was the dojo founded by Georges Stobbaerts in Casablanca in 1962, the first aikido and kendo dojo in Africa. He taught martial arts and yoga there for about a decade, forming numerous students who themselves became teachers, including Daniel Laurent and M'Barek Alaoui. It was the venue of early seminars with visiting Japanese masters such as Nobuyoshi Tamura and Julien Naessens."@en;
        schema:description      "O Budo Club du Maroc foi o dojo fundado por Georges Stobbaerts em Casablanca em 1962, o primeiro dojo de Aikido e Kendo em África. Aí ensinou artes marciais e Yoga durante cerca de uma década, formando numerosos alunos que se tornaram professores, incluindo Daniel Laurent e M'Barek Alaoui. Foi o local de estágios com mestres japoneses de visita, como Nobuyoshi Tamura e Julien Naessens."@pt;
        schema:keywords         "first-dojo-in-africa";
        schema:keywords         "aikido";
        schema:keywords         "kendo";
        schema:keywords         "casablanca";
        schema:keywords         "morocco";
        schema:name             "Budo Club du Maroc"@fr;
