<https://martial.is/entity/01KZKYMMAG9ERZ5J85WS67BH9A>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://web.archive.org/web/20260923182823/https://webhiden.jp/master/_motobu_chouki/>;
        schema:description              "Master profile of Motobu Choki on the WEB Hiden (BAB Japan) site: 1870 (Meiji 3) - 1944 (Showa 19); Ryukyu Tode karateka who brought karate to mainland Japan, most renowned for real combat of his era; late in life he named his own style Nihon Denryu Heiho Motobu Kenpo (日本伝流兵法本部拳法), commonly called Motobu-ryu karate-do. Born in Shuri Akahira as third son of Motobu Choshin of the royal blood; learned Tode with his brother from Itosu Anko, then engaged in kake-dameshi at the Tsuji quarter; studied under several masters including Matsumora Kosaku; in 1922, in Osaka, entered a boxing pick-up match and knocked out a giant Russian boxer in round two with a kosa (one-knuckle fist) strike at age 52; organized the Tode-jutsu Fukyukai in Osaka; published Okinawa Kenpo Tode Jutsu Kumite-hen (the profile dates this to 1923, differing from the 1926 date given by the Motobu-ryu official site and JA Wikipedia); moved to Tokyo in 1927, founding the Daidokan at Koishiki Haramachi, teaching at Toyo University through the mediation of Konishi Yasuhiro; published Watashi no Todejutsu in 1932; returned to Okinawa in 1939 per this profile (other sources give 1941); died spring 1944 at 74. Known for his emphasis on Naihanchi, though his books show deep knowledge of many kata."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "ja";
        schema:keywords                 "website";
        schema:keywords                 "motobu-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "karate";
        schema:name                     "本部朝基 - WEB秘伝 (達人・名人・秘伝の師範たち)";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01KZKYMMAG9ERZ5J85WS67BH9A/publisher>;
        schema:url                      <https://webhiden.jp/master/_motobu_chouki/>;
        martialis:accessed              "../2026-08-19";
        martialis:archiveDate           "2026-09-23";
        martialis:partOf                <https://martial.is/entity/01M0DCY9PEW4SQKHVV17CW6DW9>;
        martialis:peerReview            <https://w3id.org/martialis/vocab/peer-review/not_peer_reviewed>;
        martialis:sourceClassification  srcclass:authored;
        martialis:sourceType            "article-magazine" .

