<https://martial.is/entity/01M2411V8RXE6KEGH2PF8S5E1X>
        rdf:type                martialis:Style;
        schema:alternateName    "杖術"@ja;
        schema:alternateName    "Jōjutsu"@ja-Latn;
        schema:description      "Jōdō (杖道), \"way of the jō\", is a Japanese martial art using a short staff called a\njō, usually about 3 to 5 feet (0.9 to 1.5 m) long. The art is similar to bōjutsu and\nis strongly focused upon defence against the Japanese sword. It is a modern budo\nwhose origin is the koryu art Shintō Musō-ryū jōjutsu, founded by Musō Gonnosuke\nKatsuyoshi after his duels with Miyamoto Musashi; by shortening the bō to a jō of\nfour shaku two sun one bu, Gonnosuke gained the ability to combine techniques of the\nlong staff, the spear and the sword in one weapon. The older art is also known as\njōjutsu (杖術), \"art of the jō\".\n"@en;
        schema:image            <https://martial.is/entity/01M2411V8RXE6KEGH2PF8S5E1X/photos/0>;
        schema:keywords         "weapons";
        schema:keywords         "japanese-martial-arts";
        schema:keywords         "gendai";
        schema:keywords         "jodo";
        schema:name             "Jōdō"@ja-Latn;
        schema:name             "杖道"@ja;
        schema:name             "Jodo"@en;
