<https://martial.is/entity/01M5JG4Y25H7X8KYE2MFE6J1FC>
        rdf:type               martialis:Style;
        schema:alternateName   "French cane fighting"@en;
        schema:alternateName   "French staff fencing"@en;
        schema:description     "French cane and staff fencing. Practised from medieval times, it was codified by nineteenth-century masters such as Louis Leboucher and Joseph Charlemont and taught in savate clubs. It declined after the First World War; Roger Lafond revived it after the Second, and Maurice Sarry wrote competition rules. A committee within the savate federation runs it."@en;
        schema:description     "Escrime française à la canne et au bâton, codifiée au XIXe siècle par des maîtres comme Louis Leboucher et Joseph Charlemont et enseignée dans les salles de savate ; relancée après la Seconde Guerre mondiale par Roger Lafond, avec des règles de compétition de Maurice Sarry."@fr;
        schema:image           <https://martial.is/entity/01M5JG4Y25H7X8KYE2MFE6J1FC/photos/0>;
