<https://martial.is/entity/01M1BVV4WYR2KX4FZ6FP0Q7MMP>
        rdf:type                       martialis:Person;
        schema:alternateName           "Hiraoka Ryogoro"@ja-Latn;
        schema:alternateName           "平岡良五郎"@ja;
        schema:birthDate               "1837-05-13";
        schema:birthPlace              <https://martial.is/entity/01M1BVV4WYR2KX4FZ6FP0Q7MMP/birthEvent/birthPlace>;
        schema:deathDate               "1921-10-22";
        schema:deathPlace              <https://martial.is/entity/01M1BVV4WYR2KX4FZ6FP0Q7MMP/deathEvent/deathPlace>;
        schema:description             "Uchida Ryōgorō Shigeyoshi (1837-1921) was a Japanese jojutsu practitioner and holder of Menkyo Kaiden\nin the Haruyoshi branch of Shintō Musō-ryū. Born Hiraoka Ryōgorō, he was adopted into the Uchida family\nas a teenager. He founded Uchida-ryū Tanjōjutsu, a system of short staff (tanjō) techniques originally\ncalled \"Sutteki\" (stick method). He was one of only two teachers Nakayama Hakudō studied under in\n1912 at Shiba Park, Tokyo, where Hakudo learned Shintō Musō-ryū jōjutsu and valued the jo training\namong his most valuable pursuits.\n"@en;
