        rdf:type               martialis:Person;
        schema:alternateName   "Go Kenki"@ja-Latn;
        schema:description     "Tea merchant from Fuzhou who settled in Naha in 1912 and taught Fujian White Crane boxing at night above his shop. A member of the 1920s karate study groups with Chojun Miyagi, Kenwa Mabuni and Shinko Matayoshi; he gave the Nipai (Neipai) kata to Mabuni and Kyoda and was Miyagi's interpreter on his 1936 trip to China. Cramer gives 1886–1940."@en;
