<https://martial.is/entity/01KZGNJXBNDQ293MDCS5VX95VJ>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <http://web.archive.org/web/20260822223853/https://iogkf.com/senei-higaonna-kanryo/>;
        schema:description              "IOGKF (International Okinawan Goju-Ryu Karate-do Federation) biography of Kanryo Higaonna (1853-1915). Born in Naha 1853, one of eight children; his father traded firewood between the local islands. Began learning Chinese kempo at fourteen; at sixteen left for Foochow (Fuzhou), staying at the Ryukyu-kan settlement, and after nearly a year was introduced to and eventually accepted as personal disciple of Master Ryu Ryuko; helped his master as a bamboo craftsman by day and trained at night, beginning with Sanchin, nigiri-game, muchi-ishi and makiwara practice."@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "en";
        schema:keywords                 "goju-ryu";
        schema:keywords                 "karate";
