<https://martial.is/entity/01M0AJNJHSV6RHCNNKNM0Y1EHT>
        rdf:type                        martialis:Source;
        schema:archivedAt               <https://web.archive.org/web/20260515170854/http://bartitsusociety.com/new-discoveries-and-speculations-re-the-submission-grappling-of-british-jiu-jitsu/>;
        schema:datePublished            "2016";
        schema:description              "Research article by Bartitsu historian Tony Wolf (originally published on bartitsu.org, 14 Sep 2016) on the\n\"mixed styles\" submission grappling matches of London c.1900 and their roots. Identifies K. Tani (Kaneo Tani, son\nof Tenshin Shin'yo-ryu sensei Torao Tani) and S. Yamamoto as Bartitsu Club principals alongside Yukio Tani and\nSadakazu Uyenishi; documents Yataro Handa's Osaka dojo (opened 1897, teaching a Sekiguchi-ryu-derived Daito-ryu)\nas the training ground of Uyenishi, Yamamoto and Taro Miyake; attributes the ne-waza innovations largely to\nMataemon \"Newaza\" Tanabe - quoting Tanabe's own account of his development, the historian Minoru Yamada on Tanabe\nteaching both Yukio Tani and Taro Miyake at the Senbukan dojo in Kobe during the 1890s, and judo historian\nShinichi Oimatsu that \"Tani was a student of Tanabe Mataemon in Kobe\" - notes the 1891 loss of Takizaburo Tobari\nto Tanabe, and records that most of E.W. Barton-Wright's martial-arts training was done in Kobe at the Shinden\nFudo-ryu dojo of sensei Terajima Kuniichiro for about three years (c.1895-1898). Heavily relied upon by Brough et\nal. (2023, mas.166).\n"@en;
        schema:inLanguage               "en";
        schema:keywords                 "united-kingdom";
        schema:keywords                 "bartitsu";
        schema:keywords                 "jujutsu";
        schema:keywords                 "history";
        schema:keywords                 "newaza";
        schema:name                     "New Discoveries and Speculations re. the Submission Grappling of British Jiu-Jitsu";
        schema:publisher                <https://martial.is/entity/01M0AJNJHSV6RHCNNKNM0Y1EHT/publisher>;
        schema:url                      <https://bartitsusociety.com/new-discoveries-and-speculations-re-the-submission-grappling-of-british-jiu-jitsu/>;
        martialis:accessed              "2026-10-18";
        martialis:archiveDate           "2026-05-15";
        martialis:earliestYear          2016;
